my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
first line
second line
third line
END_CODE

{
    desc => '3p pastes 3 copies of yanked text below',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/count_paste_3p`

Tests `yy` followed by `3p` which yanks the current line then pastes
3 copies below it.

Keys: `yy` then `3p`

- **count_paste_3p_initial.png**: Three lines of text, cursor at line 1 col 0.
- **count_paste_3p_after_yy.png**: Line 1 yanked (intermediate state, looks same as initial).
- **count_paste_3p_after_3p.png**: Line 1 (`first line`) duplicated 3 times below.
Buffer now has 6 lines. Cursor on the last pasted line (line 4).
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('yy');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_yy');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('3p');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_3p');
    },
}
